          "note": "The whole house from the K16 kit (T-3723, piece 1 of T-1930), refined from the district draft in place under the draft's id. READ from the 1911 sheet 35 raster at full size (0.1858 m a pixel), carried into the draft's lot plan frame through the committed trace's fit (the one s35fp-2125-b1 stands on), u from the main rear wall toward Prairie and v from the north wall toward the south: the main body 10.83 m deep and 7.89 m along the avenue (columns 918-976, rows 1379-1421; the draft's fitted rectangle, 10.0 by 7.5 m, stopped short of the front and south walls), marked '2BB'; the one-storey porch marked '1' across the whole front, 1.46 m deep (to column 910), its outer edge dashed (open); on the north flank a square-sided projection 2.79 m along the wall and 0.93 m out (columns 947.5-962.5, out to row 1373.5); on the south flank a canted bay 2.98 m across at the wall, 1.95 m across its face and 1.12 m out (columns 954.5-970.5, out to row 1427); behind the main body the one-storey range marked '1BB', 6.27 m deep and 5.39 m wide (columns 976-1010, rows 1384-1413), and south of it the one-storey porch marked '1' (rows 1413-1421), its outer edge dashed. RECONSTRUCTED and recorded as L-k16-2125-frame-3723: no picture of the house is known, so everything the plan does not fix is the kit's and the reconstruction rules' — the 1.0 m raised basement, storeys of 3.3 and 3.1 m, every opening (cased two-over-two sash; three bays on the front with the four-panel door at its north end under the porch; an attic light in each gable), the bracketed eave, the 40-degree gable to the avenue (the draft's roof), both bays carried to the main body's eave (the sheet prints no count on either), the stair-hall reading of the square projection beside the door's end of the house, the range's flat deck, the one brick stack and the olive-drab body with cream trim. Not built: the rear porch south of the range (the kit builds one porch, the street one)."
